    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 passing).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `ownerSegment` following the codebase's established pattern for derived owner fields (`@Transient` getter + `readOnly` OpenAPI property \u2192 MapStruct auto-maps by name).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **New `OwnerSegment` helper** (`model/OwnerSegment.java`) \u2014 a small single-responsibility classifier mirroring `AgeBand`. Given a membership level and locality it returns `<TIER>_<AREA>`:\n   - TIER = `PREMIUM` when level \u2265 3, else `STANDARD`\n   - AREA = `METRO` when the locality is a known region, else `REGIONAL`. It reuses the existing `CityRegion.UNKNOWN` sentinel to decide \"known region\" rather than re-listing NSW/VIC/QLD, so the known-region set stays defined in one place.\n\n2. **`Owner.getOwnerSegment()`** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 a `@Transient` getter delegating to `OwnerSegment.classify(...)`, using the existing `getLocality()` derivation. No mapper change needed (name-based auto-mapping).\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared `ownerSegment` as a `readOnly` string property on the `Owner` schema so it's generated onto `OwnerDto` and serialized in responses.\n\nBoth new acceptance tests pass (Sydney/level-2 \u2192 `STANDARD_METRO`; unknown city \u2192 `STANDARD_REGIONAL`), and the full suite builds green.",
